  "notes": "Composed of {推|すい} (conjecture, infer) + {理|り} (logic, reason). Refers to logical reasoning from evidence — most commonly associated with detective fiction and mystery genres.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {推理|すいり}{小説|しょうせつ}: mystery novel, detective fiction\n- {推理|すいり}ドラマ: mystery drama/show\n- {推理|すいり}する: to reason, to deduce\n- {推理|すいり}{力|りょく}: reasoning ability\n- {鋭|するど}い{推理|すいり}: sharp deduction\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {推測|すいそく}: guess, conjecture (less rigorous, more speculative)\n- {推定|すいてい}: estimation, presumption (more objective, often statistical)\n- {論理|ろんり}: logic (abstract and academic, not detective-related)",
